itation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van&#x02019;t Hof</surname><given-names>AW</given-names></name><name><surname>Liem</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Suryapranata</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Angiographic assessment of myocardial reperfusion in patients treated with primary angioplasty for acute myocardial infarction: myocardial blush grade. Zwolle Myocardial Infarction Study Group.</article-title><source>Circulation</source><year>1998</year>;<volume>97</volume>:<fpage>2302</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9639373</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Henriques</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Zijlstra</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Ottervanger</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Incidence and clinical significance of distal embolization during primary angioplasty for acute myocardial infarction.</article-title><source>Eur Heart J</source><year>2002</year>;<volume>23</volume>:<fpage>1112</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>17</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12090749</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gy&#x000f6;ngy&#x000f6;si</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Domanovits</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Benzer</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> , <collab>and the ReoPro-BRIDGING Study Group</collab> <article-title>Use of abciximab prior to primary angioplasty in STEMI results in early recanalization of the infarct-related artery and improved myocardial tissue reperfusion&#x02014;results of the Austrian multi-centre randomized ReoPro-BRIDGING Study.</article-title><source>Eur Heart J</source><year>2004</year>;<volume>25</volume>:<fpage>2125</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>33</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15571828</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maioli</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bellandi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Leoncini</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Randomized early versus late abciximab in acute myocardial infarction treated with primary coronary intervention (RELAx-AMI Trial).</article-title><source>J Am Coll Cardiol</source><year>2007</year>;<volume>49</volume>:<fpage>1517</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>24</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17418289</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rakowski</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Zalewski</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Legutko</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Early abciximab administration before primary percutaneous coronary intervention improves infarct-related artery patency and left ventricular function in high-risk patients with anterior wall myocardial infarction: a randomized study.</article-title><source>Am Heart J</source><year>2007</year>;<volume>153</volume>:<fpage>360</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17307412</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gabriel</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name><name><surname>Oliveira</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>da Silva</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Early administration of abciximab bolus in the emergency department improves angiographic outcome after primary PCI as assessed by TIMI frame count: results of the early ReoPro administration in myocardial infarction (ERAMI) trial.</article-title><source>Catheter Cardiovasc Interv</source><year>2006</year>;<volume>68</volume>:<fpage>218</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>24</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16817177</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zorman</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Zorman</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Noc</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Effects of abciximab pretreatment in patients with acute myocardial infarction undergoing primary angioplasty.</article-title><source>Am J Cardiol</source><year>2002</year>;<volume>90</volume>:<fpage>533</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12208418</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Arntz</surname><given-names>HR</given-names></name><name><surname>Schroder</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Schwimmbeck</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Is early prehospital administration of abciximab superior to periprocedural theapy in patients with STEMI and planned PCI? Early and late results from the randomized REOMOBILE Pilot study.</article-title><source>JACC</source><year>2004</year>;<volume>43</volume><issue>Suppl A</issue></citation></ref><ref id="b19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cutlip</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Ricciardi</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ling</surname><given-names>FS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Effect of tirofiban before primary angioplasty on initial coronary flow and early ST-segment resolution in patients with acute myocardial infarction.</article-title><source>Am J Cardiol</source><year>2003</year>;<volume>92</volume>:<fpage>977</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>80</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14556878</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van&#x02019;t Hof</surname><given-names>AW</given-names></name><name><surname>Ernst</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>de Boer</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> , <collab>and the On-TIME study group</collab> <article-title>Facilitation of primary coronary angioplasty by early start of a glycoprotein 2b/3a inhibitor: results of the ongoing tirofiban in myocardial infarction evaluation (On-TIME) trial.</article-title><source>Eur Heart J</source><year>2004</year>;<volume>25</volume>:<fpage>837</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>46</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15140531</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Emre</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ucer</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Yesilcimen</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Impact of early tirofiban on myocardial salvage in patients with acute myocardial infarction undergoing infarct-related artery stenting.</article-title><source>Cardiology</source><year>2006</year>;<volume>106</volume>:<fpage>264</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16717465</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zeymer</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><n